<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Privacy Policy | WorkFlowX</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/privacy.css">
</head>

<body>

    <div class="privacy-container">

        <div class="privacy-header">
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p>Last Updated: October 5, 2026</p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-content">

            <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>
                When you use WorkFlowX, we may collect information such as
                your name, email address, account information, user role,
                tasks, requests, deadlines, and workflow activity.
            </p>

            <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <p>
                We use this information to provide task management,
                workflow management, notifications, analytics, and
                account-related services.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Account Security</h2>
            <p>
                WorkFlowX uses authentication and session mechanisms to
                help protect your account. Users should keep their
                login credentials confidential.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Task and Workflow Data</h2>
            <p>
                Task information may be visible according to the user's
                role within WorkFlowX.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>Employees can view their assigned tasks.</li>
                <li>Managers can create, assign, and monitor tasks.</li>
                <li>Admins can manage users and administrative information.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>5. Notifications</h2>
            <p>
                WorkFlowX may generate notifications for task activity,
                including overdue tasks and workflow updates.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Cookies and Sessions</h2>
            <p>
                WorkFlowX may use sessions and necessary cookies to
                maintain authentication and provide essential functionality.
            </p>

            <h2>7. Data Protection</h2>
            <p>
                We take reasonable measures to protect user information
                from unauthorized access, alteration, or disclosure.
            </p>

            <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>
                This Privacy Policy may be updated when WorkFlowX introduces
                new features or changes its services.
            </p>

            <h2>9. Contact</h2>
            <p>
                If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please
                contact the WorkFlowX administrator.
            </p>

        </div>

        <div class="privacy-footer">
            <a href="/auth/login">← Back to Login</a>
        </div>

    </div>

</body>
</html>